<details class='explain'>
<summary>Explain E030</summary>
<pre>The type of an expression does not match the expected type.

This error occurs when a value is assigned to a variable, passed as an argument,
or returned from a function with a different type than expected.

Example:
  def foo() -&gt; Int&lt;32&gt; {
    return &quot;hello&quot;;  // error: expected Int&lt;32&gt;, found &amp;Str
  }

Fix: ensure the expression has the correct type, or add an explicit cast.</pre>
